{"reference":"Zephaniah 2","book":"Zephaniah","chapter":2,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"chapter_overview","title":"Overview","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"The chapter begins with an urgent summons before the day of the LORD’s anger. The people addressed in verses 1–3 are described in difficult terms, but the call to the humble is clear: seek the LORD, righteousness, and humility. The statement that they “may be hid” presents preservation as a possibility, not an unconditional guarantee.","verse_refs":["Zephaniah 2:1-3"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_zephaniah_002_1ed21dca49c8f1c1ab6e466b"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"},{"id":"block_2","text":"The judgment then reaches outward: the Philistine coast and its cities, Moab and Ammon, the Cushites, and Assyria with Nineveh. The coast is pictured as emptied and becoming pasture for Judah’s remnant; Moab and Ammon are condemned for reproach and pride; Cush is addressed only briefly, without identifying its precise scope; and Nineveh is imagined as a desolate place inhabited by animals. The sequence gives the chapter a broad horizon of judgment while retaining distinct reasons and images for particular peoples and places.","verse_refs":["Zephaniah 2:4-7","Zephaniah 2:8-11","Zephaniah 2:12","Zephaniah 2:13-15"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_zephaniah_002_67a93ddc5319c6248fedab05"],"confidence":"medium","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]},{"kind":"historical_context","title":"Nineveh and Assyria","blocks":[{"id":"block_3","text":"Nineveh’s ruin is set against sources that portray Assyrian imperial self-presentation through palaces, gardens, cult, tribute, conquest, and royal ideology. Those royal inscriptions are valuable for understanding how Assyria represented itself, though they are not neutral accounts of all late Assyrian society. A Babylonian chronicle records Nineveh’s fall in 612 BCE and Harran’s in 609 BCE, providing a historical anchor for the city’s destruction without settling the date of every part of Zephaniah.","verse_refs":["Zephaniah 2:13-15"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_zephaniah_002_aac671be42eecb6d3950aaa1","reader_path_zephaniah_002_cb3d67d5c3afa1fb710b0cb5"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"fact"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}